#import "template.typ": policy-rule, policy-warning

= Remote Work, Equipment & Office Supplies

== Routine Office Supplies

Employees working remotely or traveling may occasionally need incidental office supplies to perform essential duties.

#policy-rule("POL-EQP-001", "Routine Office Supplies Cap")[
  Incidental stationery, notebooks, pens, and printer paper may be expensed up to €50.00 / \$60.00 per purchase, not to exceed €100.00 / \$120.00 per quarter. Where possible, standard corporate procurement catalogues should be used instead of retail out-of-pocket purchases.
]

== Computer Peripherals and Hardware

All computer hardware and digital devices remain company property and must comply with IT security protocols.

#policy-rule("POL-EQP-002", "IT Hardware Peripherals Approval")[
  Hardware peripherals (monitors, keyboards, external hard drives, noise-canceling headsets, webcams) exceeding €100.00 / \$120.00 require written authorization from the IT Operations Department prior to purchase. Ergonomic furniture, office desks, and chairs are non-reimbursable through standard travel expense reports.
]

== Software Licenses & Cloud Subscriptions

Unauthorized software subscriptions present severe information security and compliance risks.

#policy-warning("POL-EQP-003", "Software and SaaS Centralization")[
  Employees must not expense software licenses, SaaS subscriptions, cloud hosting credits, or AI model API credits through out-of-pocket expense reports without explicit written pre-approval from Enterprise IT and Information Security.
]
